=== SR10 config-edit SKILL.md ===
3:description: Edit workloom config fields in a user project — config.json, config.js, config.local.json, config.local.js — through a five-step discipline and the on-disk field whitelist. Triggers on config field edits (packages, worktree, hooks, subagent_profiles, context_injection, prompt_injection, executor, session_auto_commit, coverage); package-structure scanning stays with workloom-packages-scan.
9:Edit workloom configuration in the user's project through a fixed five-step discipline. On-disk keys are snake_case; `loadConfig` converts them to the camelCase runtime shape. The [disk field whitelist](#disk-field-whitelist) is the enforcement point for unknown top-level keys, because `loadConfig` ignores them silently.
5
25:| `packages` | map of name to `{ path, setup?, type?, git? }` |
26:| `worktree` | `{ enabled?, branch_template?, cleanup? }` |
27:| `hooks` | `{ after_create?, after_start?, after_finish?, after_archive? }`, each a string array |
28:| `subagent_profiles` | array of `{ whenMain?, roles }` |
29:| `context_injection` | `{ max_file_bytes?, max_artifact_bytes?, max_total_bytes? }` |
30:| `prompt_injection` | `{ skip_keyword? }` |
31:| `executor` | `{ max_concurrent? }` |
32:| `session_auto_commit` | boolean |
33:| `coverage` | `{ threshold?, languages? }` — see [Coverage configuration](#coverage-configuration) |
41:The only accepted command placeholders are `<worktree>` (task worktree root), `<profile>` (coverage report output path), and `<base-ref>` (baseline branch). Any other token fails validation. For example:
59:- Edit only the project layer (`.workloom/config.json` or `.workloom/config.js`) and the local layer (`.workloom/config.local.json` or `.workloom/config.local.js`). Global config under `$HOME/.workloom/` is out of scope; route it to `workloom-migrate-to-sop`.
39:`coverage.threshold` is an integer from 0 to 100 (default 90). The gate requires incremental coverage to be strictly greater than it. `coverage.languages` maps a language name to `{ format, command? }`; `format` must be one of `go-coverprofile`, `lcov`, `jacoco-xml`, or `cobertura-xml`. Built-in languages need no entry — they fall back to `LANGUAGE_DEFAULTS`. An unknown subfield, an invalid format, or an unknown `<…>` placeholder in `command` is rejected by `loadConfig`.
